// Shared build configuration consumed by iosApp.xcodeproj.
APP_NAME = SnapSync
BUNDLE_ID = app.snapsync
// Public version (CFBundleShortVersionString), inherited by BOTH the app and the background-upload
// extension targets (this is the project-level base config; neither target pins a target-level
// MARKETING_VERSION any more). This value is the version FLOOR, two-part `X.Y`, seeded at 0.1. It is
// what a plain/local build carries, and the seed a main/internal build carries before any release tag
// exists. ios.yml COMPUTES the version each main build actually carries as
//   MARKETING_VERSION = max(this floor, latest vX.Y tag with its minor incremented by 1)
// (integer minor bump — 0.9→0.10, never a decimal carry to 1.0 — compared as (major,minor) tuples),
// so builds auto-advance off the last release tag. The floor is normally left alone; bump it here (via
// a PR) ONLY to force a MAJOR jump, e.g. 0.1 → 1.0. There is no longer an App Store "trap": main builds
// reach only the internal TestFlight group (no Beta App Review at any version), and the App Store release
// channel (ios-appstore-release / .github/workflows/ios-appstore-promote.yml) PROMOTES an existing build
// and derives the store version FROM it — it never overrides MARKETING_VERSION and never builds.
// ⚠️ Do NOT set the Version field in Xcode's target → General tab: Xcode would write a target-level
// MARKETING_VERSION back into project.pbxproj, shadowing this value again.
MARKETING_VERSION = 0.1
// Apple Team ID — drives DEVELOPMENT_TEAM for signed device/TestFlight builds.
// Not a secret (visible in any shipped IPA); the simulator gate ignores it (CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO).
TEAM_ID = E9Z8BADH58
// Entitlements (path relative to SRCROOT = iosApp/): keychain-sharing (event-link), the App
// Group group.app.snapsync (the background-upload extension's shared ledger container), and the
// associated domain for the event link (below). Keychain groups need no portal registration; the App
// Group and Associated Domains DO — each must be registered in the Developer portal and enabled on the
// app.snapsync App ID, or signed device/TestFlight builds fail to provision (see the
// ios-background-upload change, task 2.x). The simulator gate ignores signing.
CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS = iosApp/iosApp.entitlements
// The event link's associated domain (capability `event-link`), consumed by the app's
// com.apple.developer.associated-domains entitlement. The host MUST match `snapsync.domain` in
// gradle.properties (which generates the app's LINK_ORIGIN) and the AASA the backend serves from its
// own constant — nothing in the build can reach `backend/`, so a :test:architecture guard asserts all
// of them agree. Drift is SILENT: iOS simply declines to match the link and every invite opens Safari,
// which looks exactly like a recipient who never installed the app.
// Plain `applinks:` deliberately — no `?mode=developer` dev/prod split (unlike APS_ENVIRONMENT below):
// Apple's cached copy is directly readable at
// https://app-site-association.cdn-apple.com/a/v1/<domain>, so CDN staleness is one curl away from
// being diagnosed rather than an invisible multi-hour wait.
ASSOCIATED_DOMAIN = applinks:snapsync.stho.net
// The compile-time upload host (PhotoKit forces BackgroundUploadURLBase to be baked, not runtime).
// This is the SINGLE SOURCE of the deployed device-facing host: `snapsync.stho.net`, a custom domain
// WE control via Bunny DNS, CNAME'd to the bunny pull zone fronting the Edge Script. Because we own the
// name, swapping the backend runtime is a DNS repoint — NOT a new build — so this literal MUST stay
// a domain we control, never a runtime-provider vanity host. (That property is what made retiring Deno
// Deploy a DNS flip instead of a forced TestFlight round; see openspec/specs/backend-deployment.)
// A plain *local* Xcode build and every
// plain push/TestFlight build target it (CI does NOT restate the literal — it overrides only when a
// workflow_dispatch `upload_host` is supplied, which must be HTTPS). Must be HTTPS: default ATS
// (HTTPS-only) applies — no NSAllowsLocalNetworking exception ships. The `$()` splits the `//` so
// xcconfig does not treat the rest of the line as a comment (CLI overrides need no such trick).
BACKGROUND_UPLOAD_URL_BASE = https:/$()/snapsync.stho.net
// APNs environment (capability `push-registration`). APS_ENVIRONMENT drives the aps-environment
// entitlement; APNS_ENV is baked into Info.plist and read by the app so its device config reports which
// APNs host the token belongs to. They MUST agree: `development`+`sandbox` for a plain local/dev build
// (the sideload loop uses the APNs sandbox), `production`+`production` for TestFlight/App Store. CI
// overrides both for a distribution build (as it can override the upload host); a plain build stays dev.
APS_ENVIRONMENT = development
APNS_ENV = sandbox
// Crash reporting (capability `crash-reporting`). Both values are baked into BOTH targets'
// Info.plists and read by the CrashReporting adapter. The DSN default is EMPTY on purpose —
// absence is the off-switch (no SDK starts, no connection opens); only a CI Release archive
// injects the real value from the SENTRY_DSN secret (capability `ios-testflight-delivery`),
// alongside SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT=production. A dev build that deliberately injects a DSN (the
// on-device verification loop) keeps `development` here and reports honestly.
SENTRY_DSN =
SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT = development
